<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Killala</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Killala is a village and small port on Killala Bay in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-mayo">County Mayo</a>, in the west of Ireland, and the seat of an ancient bishopric. On 22 August 1798 a French force under General Jean Humbert landed there to support the rebellion of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/society-of-united-irishmen">United Irishmen</a>; after early success at Castlebar it surrendered at Ballinamuck, and government troops retook the town.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/killala.jpg" alt="Killala" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Liz McCabe · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Killala_street_scene_-_geograph.org.uk_-_486739.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
